1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:02,712
And he's ready, Señor.

2
00:00:04,271 --> 00:00:06,273
A big change can be worthwhile.

3
00:00:06,273 --> 00:00:10,158
And I just hope I can make you all proud
with this new project.

4
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:15,449
- Liam!
- Yes, you changed your life.

5
00:00:15,449 --> 00:00:18,986
You rise to the top while we die one by one.

6
00:00:18,986 --> 00:00:21,322
You should die before anyone else does!

7
00:00:21,322 --> 00:00:24,124
Why did you do that to me?
I really can't remember anything.

8
00:00:24,124 --> 00:00:29,229
You dazzled us with money that's so small
compared to what you'll gain.

9
00:00:29,229 --> 00:00:33,334
You tore down
almost half of our neighborhood.

10
00:00:33,334 --> 00:00:36,403
And you stole our livelihood!

11
00:00:36,403 --> 00:00:39,073
Nestor Bartolome.

12
00:00:39,073 --> 00:00:41,942
A resident of Verde Village.

13
00:00:44,345 --> 00:00:49,083
The community
beside Casa Fuerte's Strongland Residences?

14
00:00:49,083 --> 00:00:51,185
But that's how furious they are to me?

15
00:00:51,185 --> 00:00:53,954
What did I do wrong to them?

16
00:00:53,954 --> 00:00:55,888
Boss, I'm begging you.

17
00:00:55,888 --> 00:00:57,624
Please, don't put my grandfather in prison.

18
00:00:57,624 --> 00:00:59,026
Jail me instead.

19
00:00:59,026 --> 00:01:01,462
If you need to imprison someone,
let it be me.

20
00:01:01,462 --> 00:01:04,732
If you did something wrong,
I know there was a reason behind it.

21
00:01:04,732 --> 00:01:06,734
Liam, you taught me

22
00:01:06,734 --> 00:01:09,336
that everyone can have a second chance,

23
00:01:09,336 --> 00:01:13,035
just like how you gave me
my second chance at happiness.

24
00:01:40,501 --> 00:01:42,669
<i>This time...</i>

25
00:01:42,669 --> 00:01:47,316
<i>showing your weakness is not cowardice.</i>

26
00:01:48,293 --> 00:01:53,824
<i>I thought everything would be better
if you were here.</i>

27
00:02:01,755 --> 00:02:07,994
<i>Sometimes, life brings us
to an unexpected path.</i>

28
00:02:10,898 --> 00:02:13,700
<i>To an uncertain place.</i>

29
00:02:15,269 --> 00:02:18,572
<i>We don't know if it will lead us astray</i>

30
00:02:18,572 --> 00:02:22,542
<i>or if it will bring us
to the right destination.</i>

31
00:02:23,710 --> 00:02:26,547
This is it. There's no turning back.

32
00:02:26,547 --> 00:02:28,148
If you say so.

33
00:02:29,716 --> 00:02:33,787
Liam Herrera, are you having second thoughts?

34
00:02:33,787 --> 00:02:35,923
I just don't want to get rejected again.

35
00:02:35,923 --> 00:02:38,025
They already turned this story down.

36
00:02:38,025 --> 00:02:40,027
Wait, hold on.

37
00:02:40,027 --> 00:02:45,232
You know...
They haven't read your whole story yet.

38
00:02:45,232 --> 00:02:47,901
Yet they turned it down in just one call?

39
00:02:47,901 --> 00:02:49,036
That's wrong.

40
00:02:49,036 --> 00:02:56,110
So, they should read the whole pilot script.

41
00:02:56,110 --> 00:02:58,144
So what do we do?

42
00:02:59,046 --> 00:03:03,784
All the pilot scripts for review
are in the executive producer's office.

43
00:03:03,784 --> 00:03:09,890
So we will include your script with the rest.

44
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:12,493
How do we get inside the producer's office?

45
00:03:12,493 --> 00:03:14,908
We don't have access here.

46
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:18,899
Where did you get that?

47
00:03:18,899 --> 00:03:21,902
Well, in case you forgot,

48
00:03:21,902 --> 00:03:25,739
I've played bit roles in this TV network
many times.

49
00:03:25,739 --> 00:03:28,075
So, I have connections.

50
00:03:28,075 --> 00:03:30,410
Is that legal?

51
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:32,666
Let's just say

52
00:03:32,667 --> 00:03:36,583
that you will become
one of the greatest writers

53
00:03:36,583 --> 00:03:39,686
this TV network has known.

54
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:43,924
So let's go. You're gonna have to wear this.

55
00:03:43,924 --> 00:03:46,760
Don't show my photo.
Just pretend it's your ID.

56
00:03:46,760 --> 00:03:48,428
I'm famous here.

57
00:03:48,428 --> 00:03:49,830
My face will be enough.

58
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:51,265
Let's go!

59
00:03:51,265 --> 00:03:52,866
Really?

60
00:03:55,335 --> 00:03:57,103
- This is what we'll do.
- What?

61
00:03:57,971 --> 00:03:59,673
Over there is the office of Sir Mark, okay?

62
00:03:59,673 --> 00:04:02,543
I'll distract the guard.
Just wait for my signal, okay?

63
00:04:02,543 --> 00:04:04,377
Isn't that dangerous?

64
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:16,023
Ma'am, where are you going?

65
00:04:16,023 --> 00:04:17,558
Joyce.

66
00:04:17,558 --> 00:04:20,294
- Trinidad.
- Joyce!

67
00:04:20,294 --> 00:04:21,795
- So it's you.
- Meynard.

68
00:04:21,795 --> 00:04:24,965
It's me.
How can you forget my beautiful face?

69
00:04:24,965 --> 00:04:28,001
- How are you?
- What are you doing here?

70
00:04:28,001 --> 00:04:29,469
Meynard...

71
00:04:29,469 --> 00:04:31,972
I'm just visiting.

72
00:04:31,972 --> 00:04:34,208
You just finished taping your show, right?

73
00:04:34,208 --> 00:04:35,475
Yes.

74
00:04:35,475 --> 00:04:38,345
Did you watch our episode last night?

75
00:04:38,345 --> 00:04:39,813
It was great.

76
00:04:39,813 --> 00:04:41,481
- You were really great.
- I know, right?

77
00:04:41,481 --> 00:04:42,749
- Yes.
- I knew it.

78
00:04:42,749 --> 00:04:45,635
I deserve a better role
than "classmate number two", right?

79
00:04:45,635 --> 00:04:47,821
I should play the best friend.

80
00:04:47,821 --> 00:04:48,889
Joyce...

81
00:04:48,889 --> 00:04:52,025
Don't forget about me once you become a star.

82
00:04:52,025 --> 00:04:53,360
Of course, Meynard.

83
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:55,829
You're one of my favorites.
With your good looks...

84
00:04:55,829 --> 00:04:57,664
There's someone. Meynard...

85
00:04:57,664 --> 00:04:59,499
- Oh, he doesn't have an ID.
- Yes?

86
00:04:59,499 --> 00:05:01,068
- I wonder what he needs.
- Where are you going?

87
00:05:01,068 --> 00:05:02,869
Seventh floor, Sir.

88
00:05:03,503 --> 00:05:04,738
Who are you looking for?

89
00:05:04,738 --> 00:05:07,774
Well, I'm looking for Melvin.

90
00:05:12,079 --> 00:05:15,281
Come on, hurry up. Someone might see us.

91
00:05:16,559 --> 00:05:17,766
- Go.
- What do you mean?

92
00:05:17,767 --> 00:05:20,133
- Put it there.
- Should I?

93
00:05:20,133 --> 00:05:23,661
I'm sure that if Sir Mark reads your script,

94
00:05:23,661 --> 00:05:25,859
he'll approve it.

95
00:05:25,859 --> 00:05:27,694
He'll hire you as a writer.
You'll be a regular here.

96
00:05:27,694 --> 00:05:30,601
They will produce your script, have a shoot,
and air it right away.

97
00:05:30,601 --> 00:05:32,733
Then that's it!

98
00:05:32,733 --> 00:05:33,967
You think?

99
00:05:33,967 --> 00:05:35,636
Of course!

100
00:05:35,636 --> 00:05:38,371
I believe in you.

101
00:05:39,973 --> 00:05:43,076
You're the only one who encourages me.

102
00:05:45,279 --> 00:05:46,780
Go. Do it.

103
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:48,982
- Here?
- Yes.

104
00:06:17,110 --> 00:06:19,345
I thought someone was here.

105
00:06:30,957 --> 00:06:33,561
I thought we would get caught.

106
00:06:39,433 --> 00:06:41,701
We weren't caught, but...

107
00:06:42,436 --> 00:06:44,371
We're locked in.

108
00:06:44,371 --> 00:06:45,372
What?

109
00:06:45,372 --> 00:06:48,275
See? It won't open.

110
00:06:48,275 --> 00:06:50,410
How do we get out of here?

111
00:07:01,021 --> 00:07:06,126
<i>And in this world where I feel trapped...</i>

112
00:07:06,126 --> 00:07:09,662
<i>I'm thankful that I found you again.</i>

113
00:07:36,189 --> 00:07:38,392
Joyce.

114
00:07:38,392 --> 00:07:39,940
Joyce.

115
00:07:46,486 --> 00:07:49,315
Joyce, I thought you weren't in this world.

116
00:07:54,955 --> 00:07:56,723
You're getting married?

117
00:07:57,677 --> 00:07:59,779
Who are you marrying?

118
00:08:04,451 --> 00:08:07,053
- Joy...
- Do I know you?

119
00:08:07,854 --> 00:08:09,790
Cut! My God, cut!

120
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:11,625
- What are you doing?
- Who's that guy?

121
00:08:11,625 --> 00:08:16,029
- This is crazy!
- He ruined the scene.

122
00:08:16,029 --> 00:08:19,065
Who's this guy messing with my set?

123
00:08:19,065 --> 00:08:22,368
This is disappointing.

124
00:08:22,368 --> 00:08:24,016
A set?

125
00:08:25,605 --> 00:08:27,607
Yes, Mister. We're in a middle of a scene.

126
00:08:27,607 --> 00:08:29,475
We're filming.

127
00:08:31,044 --> 00:08:33,079
Filming?

128
00:08:33,079 --> 00:08:35,581
Joyce, what's this?

129
00:08:37,050 --> 00:08:40,587
Savana, do you know him?

130
00:08:40,587 --> 00:08:43,490
I'm sorry, Director. I don't know him.

131
00:08:43,490 --> 00:08:45,625
Savana?

132
00:08:45,625 --> 00:08:46,793
What do you mean by "director"?

133
00:08:46,793 --> 00:08:49,796
Yes, I'm the film director.

134
00:08:49,796 --> 00:08:51,398
She's Savana.

135
00:08:51,398 --> 00:08:55,669
And you're the pest
who's interrupting our set.

136
00:08:55,669 --> 00:08:57,804
Where's crowd control? Crowd control!

137
00:08:57,804 --> 00:08:59,072
Come!

138
00:08:59,072 --> 00:09:00,941
Hurry up!

139
00:09:00,941 --> 00:09:02,242
Get him out of here.

140
00:09:02,242 --> 00:09:06,179
I told you already.
We're doing it again and again.

141
00:09:08,315 --> 00:09:10,083
- Arvie!
- Yes, Director?

142
00:09:10,083 --> 00:09:11,418
- From the top.
- Okay, Director.

143
00:09:11,418 --> 00:09:13,286
- My God!
- Sorry, Director.

144
00:09:13,286 --> 00:09:14,754
Okay, guys. Places.

145
00:09:14,754 --> 00:09:16,856
From the top.

146
00:09:27,367 --> 00:09:29,135
Talents!

147
00:09:29,135 --> 00:09:31,271
Talents, hurry up! Fall in line.

148
00:09:31,271 --> 00:09:32,905
Here.

149
00:09:36,343 --> 00:09:38,778
Savana is so beautiful, right?

150
00:09:38,778 --> 00:09:42,516
Yes, I thought she is a snob,
but she's so nice.

151
00:09:42,516 --> 00:09:44,651
And she smells good.

152
00:09:44,651 --> 00:09:48,554
I wish I'd get chosen to be her partner.

153
00:09:49,222 --> 00:09:51,725
So, you are now known as "Savana".

154
00:09:51,725 --> 00:09:53,994
That's why I can't find you.

155
00:09:53,994 --> 00:09:56,429
Her name has been Savana ever since.

156
00:10:01,334 --> 00:10:04,971
That's just her screen name, right?

157
00:10:06,139 --> 00:10:11,044
Yes, but no one knew her name
when she was not famous yet.

158
00:10:11,044 --> 00:10:13,613
She became known as Savana.

159
00:10:15,515 --> 00:10:17,984
She's now a famous actress?

160
00:10:17,984 --> 00:10:21,388
Have you been hiding under a rock
to be so clueless about Savana?

161
00:10:21,388 --> 00:10:23,381
No...

162
00:10:23,381 --> 00:10:27,051
I'm not into show business.

163
00:10:27,888 --> 00:10:31,498
Why are you here if you don't like it?

164
00:10:31,498 --> 00:10:36,249
- Right?
- Honestly, I just happened to pass by.

165
00:10:36,249 --> 00:10:40,019
I thought there was a real wedding.

166
00:10:41,341 --> 00:10:45,679
But tell me more about Savana.

167
00:10:45,679 --> 00:10:48,814
She became famous
in this drama, Captive Hearts.

168
00:10:51,217 --> 00:10:53,553
You're filming Captive Hearts?

169
00:10:53,553 --> 00:10:55,455
Yes.

170
00:10:55,455 --> 00:10:57,390
It's been running for years.

171
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:59,225
It's been on air for quite a while.

172
00:10:59,225 --> 00:11:00,894
Seven years.

173
00:11:00,894 --> 00:11:03,329
Savana's charm is really something.

174
00:11:05,398 --> 00:11:09,168
You have fulfilled your dream, Joyce.

175
00:11:09,903 --> 00:11:11,371
Guys.

176
00:11:11,371 --> 00:11:13,373
- Guys, guys, guys.
- Yes, Director?

177
00:11:13,373 --> 00:11:15,942
You're making my blood boil.

178
00:11:15,942 --> 00:11:19,999
We need to find a good-looking guy

179
00:11:19,999 --> 00:11:22,415
to be Savana's partner in the next scene.

180
00:11:22,415 --> 00:11:25,318
- Okay.
- Okay? Wait...

181
00:11:25,318 --> 00:11:27,921
I'll do it. I will choose the guy myself.

182
00:11:27,921 --> 00:11:28,922
- Okay?
- Okay.

183
00:11:28,922 --> 00:11:30,156
Where are they?

184
00:11:30,156 --> 00:11:32,125
Here.

185
00:11:32,125 --> 00:11:33,726
Okay.

186
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,969
Shrimp number one.

187
00:11:42,969 --> 00:11:43,970
Okay?

188
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:45,705
Take note.

189
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:49,575
Try. Let me try.

190
00:11:54,014 --> 00:11:55,482
Shrimp number two.

191
00:11:55,482 --> 00:11:56,783
Okay, Director.

192
00:11:56,783 --> 00:11:58,918
Okay?

193
00:11:58,918 --> 00:12:01,287
This one...

194
00:12:01,287 --> 00:12:02,656
Well, it's possible.

195
00:12:02,656 --> 00:12:07,893
But... he's shrimp number three.

196
00:12:09,429 --> 00:12:11,063
Okay?

197
00:12:12,632 --> 00:12:14,366
Mister...

198
00:12:15,327 --> 00:12:17,037
Why?

199
00:12:17,037 --> 00:12:18,605
What?

200
00:12:18,605 --> 00:12:20,373
What are you doing here?

201
00:12:20,373 --> 00:12:24,310
Guys, what do you think our show is?

202
00:12:24,310 --> 00:12:25,845
A cooking show?

203
00:12:25,845 --> 00:12:30,550
You're sending me all these shrimps.

204
00:12:30,550 --> 00:12:31,951
We'll just look for someone else.

205
00:12:31,951 --> 00:12:33,987
Look for someone else, now.

206
00:12:33,987 --> 00:12:36,155
- Hurry up.
- Hurry.

207
00:12:37,057 --> 00:12:38,824
This is driving me nuts.

208
00:12:43,997 --> 00:12:46,499
Do you know how to drive?

209
00:12:46,499 --> 00:12:48,034
Do you know how to drive?

210
00:12:48,034 --> 00:12:49,002
- Me?
- Yes.

211
00:12:49,002 --> 00:12:51,004
No, our director.

212
00:12:51,004 --> 00:12:53,439
Of course, you. I'm asking you.

213
00:12:54,741 --> 00:12:57,210
- Yes, I do. Why?
- Okay, come here.

214
00:12:57,210 --> 00:12:58,678
Come with me.

215
00:12:58,678 --> 00:13:01,013
- What?
- Come on. Come with me.

216
00:13:01,815 --> 00:13:03,416
Director, we already found someone.

217
00:13:03,416 --> 00:13:04,517
Here he is.

218
00:13:04,517 --> 00:13:05,719
He's good-looking, and he knows how to drive.

219
00:13:05,719 --> 00:13:07,821
Hold on. Wait, wait.

220
00:13:07,821 --> 00:13:13,026
Him? The guy who ruined our scene earlier?

221
00:13:13,026 --> 00:13:15,995
Yes, Director. We have no one else...

222
00:13:15,995 --> 00:13:18,364
I just happened to pass by.

223
00:13:21,367 --> 00:13:22,702
Okay.

224
00:13:22,702 --> 00:13:25,872
Let's try him.

225
00:13:25,872 --> 00:13:27,907
- Teach him the lines.
- Yes, Director.

226
00:13:27,907 --> 00:13:28,945
I don't want to do it over and over.

227
00:13:28,945 --> 00:13:31,111
I will throw some lines at him
so he can memorize them.

228
00:13:31,111 --> 00:13:32,512
- Go!
- Go, Riza. Go! Go!

229
00:13:32,512 --> 00:13:34,214
- MJ, Macy...
- Let's go.

230
00:13:34,214 --> 00:13:35,815
Put some makeup on him.

231
00:13:36,716 --> 00:13:39,052
Hey, hey.

232
00:13:39,052 --> 00:13:41,621
Hurry up.

233
00:13:41,621 --> 00:13:43,223
What?

234
00:13:43,223 --> 00:13:45,692
That's too long. I can't memorize that.

235
00:13:45,692 --> 00:13:49,895
- Go, go, go. Places, everyone.
- I can dress on my own.

236
00:14:13,887 --> 00:14:15,986
You're the man earlier, right?

237
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:22,074
Yes, Miss Savana.

238
00:14:23,363 --> 00:14:28,368
I'm sorry if I'm not myself earlier.

239
00:14:28,368 --> 00:14:31,370
The name you called me...

240
00:14:34,808 --> 00:14:38,677
- Sorry?
- You called me by a different name.

241
00:14:40,747 --> 00:14:43,449
Have we met before?

242
00:14:43,449 --> 00:14:45,743
You look familiar.

243
00:14:48,555 --> 00:14:51,424
Do you recognize me now, Jo...

244
00:14:56,329 --> 00:14:58,631
Arvie! Let's start filming.

245
00:14:58,631 --> 00:15:01,033
Stand by for take, actors!

246
00:15:01,033 --> 00:15:02,568
ID, please.

247
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:04,603
ID, Captive Hearts!

248
00:15:04,603 --> 00:15:06,572
- Rolling!
- Audio roll!

249
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:09,508
Sequence 22, take one!

250
00:15:11,477 --> 00:15:13,212
Okay, ready!

251
00:15:13,212 --> 00:15:14,446
Rolling!

252
00:15:14,446 --> 00:15:16,482
- Rolling, Director!
- In three...

253
00:15:16,482 --> 00:15:18,484
- Two...
- One...

254
00:15:18,484 --> 00:15:20,519
Action!

255
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:38,607
Say your line!

256
00:15:39,705 --> 00:15:41,677
Ma'am, are you okay?

257
00:15:44,361 --> 00:15:46,076
Yes, Mister.

258
00:16:04,730 --> 00:16:07,922
Everything happens for a reason.

259
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:19,293
What's worse...
is to spend the rest of your life with him,

260
00:16:20,512 --> 00:16:23,014
but you are not happy.

261
00:16:32,327 --> 00:16:34,293
Cut!

262
00:16:34,293 --> 00:16:35,627
Lovely!

263
00:16:35,627 --> 00:16:39,197
Cut! Good take! Next sequence!

264
00:16:54,947 --> 00:16:57,349
We love you, Savana!

265
00:16:57,349 --> 00:16:59,618
- Bye, Savana.
- Savana!

266
00:16:59,618 --> 00:17:02,654
Savana! Savana!

267
00:17:02,654 --> 00:17:04,566
Don't forget...

268
00:17:05,324 --> 00:17:07,993
Don't miss the fans' day, okay?

269
00:17:07,993 --> 00:17:10,829
Bring the tarps and everything.
See you there.

270
00:17:10,829 --> 00:17:14,058
Hashtag Savana Forever!

271
00:17:16,502 --> 00:17:18,904
Savana.

272
00:17:18,904 --> 00:17:21,407
Can we talk?

273
00:17:21,407 --> 00:17:23,575
- You again?
- Excuse me.

274
00:17:23,575 --> 00:17:26,478
Look who we have here.

275
00:17:26,478 --> 00:17:28,847
Savana's meet-and-greet isn't today.

276
00:17:28,847 --> 00:17:31,351
She's tired. She had an early call time.

277
00:17:31,351 --> 00:17:33,686
So let's go.

278
00:17:33,686 --> 00:17:35,121
Mom?

279
00:17:37,090 --> 00:17:39,491
What? What did you say?

280
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:45,369
You're beautiful in person, Aunt Joanne.

281
00:17:48,001 --> 00:17:50,803
Come on.

282
00:17:50,803 --> 00:17:52,972
Fine. I know you'll just ask for a selfie.

283
00:17:52,972 --> 00:17:54,774
Go on. You can take a selfie with her.

284
00:17:54,774 --> 00:17:58,044
Right there and right now, okay?

285
00:17:58,044 --> 00:17:59,645
Savana.

286
00:17:59,645 --> 00:18:02,377
Mister, let me have your phone.

287
00:18:04,714 --> 00:18:05,785
Just one.

288
00:18:05,785 --> 00:18:07,720
Only one picture.

289
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:13,026
- Savana!
- Savana!

290
00:18:13,026 --> 00:18:15,794
One, two, three...

291
00:18:16,996 --> 00:18:18,664
Mister, smile at the camera.

292
00:18:18,664 --> 00:18:20,333
Look at the camera.

293
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:22,468
One, two, three...

294
00:18:23,436 --> 00:18:24,637
There. Okay, done.

295
00:18:24,637 --> 00:18:26,729
Okay! Bye!

296
00:18:26,729 --> 00:18:30,143
See you at the meet-and-greet
on her fans' day.

297
00:18:30,143 --> 00:18:32,478
Be present!

298
00:18:32,478 --> 00:18:33,863
Excuse me.

299
00:18:36,749 --> 00:18:40,686
Okay! Hashtag Savana Forever, okay?

300
00:18:40,686 --> 00:18:46,893
- Savana!
- Savana!

301
00:18:46,893 --> 00:18:49,295
Give it to me.

302
00:18:49,295 --> 00:18:50,938
Savana?

303
00:18:52,198 --> 00:18:54,867
Madam, the alcohol is running out.

304
00:18:54,867 --> 00:18:58,805
They say it's not good to be so clean.

305
00:18:58,805 --> 00:19:01,074
I'm not asking for your opinion.

306
00:19:01,074 --> 00:19:02,507
Thank you.

307
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:11,316
He seems familiar to me.

308
00:19:12,718 --> 00:19:13,886
Who?

309
00:19:13,886 --> 00:19:15,955
The handsome man who asked
for a picture with you?

310
00:19:15,955 --> 00:19:19,625
What?
The one who messed up the wedding scene?

311
00:19:19,625 --> 00:19:22,195
Oh, dear. Do you have a past with him?

312
00:19:22,195 --> 00:19:25,031
It might be another stalker story.

313
00:19:25,031 --> 00:19:27,232
It will only bring trouble.

314
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:39,145
He was my classmate in college.

315
00:19:39,145 --> 00:19:41,714
He was viral last week!

316
00:19:41,714 --> 00:19:43,582
Look!

317
00:19:44,484 --> 00:19:46,285
I knew it.

318
00:19:46,285 --> 00:19:48,121
I knew it was him!

319
00:19:48,121 --> 00:19:49,255
This is him.

320
00:19:49,255 --> 00:19:53,192
He's the executive of Casa Fuerte,
who almost got stabbed.

321
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:54,627
- Let me see, let me see.
- There.

322
00:19:54,627 --> 00:19:58,064
I heard people are furious at him

323
00:19:58,064 --> 00:20:00,966
because he's a land grabber.

324
00:20:03,136 --> 00:20:06,339
Is he your college classmate, Savana?

325
00:20:06,339 --> 00:20:08,040
Assassination attempt?

326
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:09,509
Oh, gosh.

327
00:20:09,509 --> 00:20:11,110
Stay away from him.

328
00:20:11,110 --> 00:20:13,346
Stay away from people like him.

329
00:20:13,346 --> 00:20:15,348
It's a no, no, no, no situation.

330
00:20:15,348 --> 00:20:17,850
That's a no, no, no win-win situation.

331
00:20:17,850 --> 00:20:20,978
- Savana!
- Savana!

332
00:20:20,978 --> 00:20:23,317
Liam Herrera.

333
00:20:24,488 --> 00:20:26,333
Land grabber.

334
00:20:27,661 --> 00:20:31,330
- Rico, let's go.
- Okay, Ma'am Joanne.

335
00:20:31,330 --> 00:20:35,634
- Savana!
- Savana!

336
00:20:58,167 --> 00:21:15,200
[Savana Famous Actress in the Philippines]

337
00:21:16,067 --> 00:21:22,534
[Savana pics]

338
00:21:23,367 --> 00:21:30,976
[Savana TV and Movies]

339
00:21:30,977 --> 00:21:34,586
<i>I feel like I'm just your sister's puppet.</i>

340
00:21:35,528 --> 00:21:38,331
<i>Don't worry.</i>

341
00:21:38,331 --> 00:21:41,467
<i>My sister loves you.</i>

342
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:44,000
<i>I wish she was as kind as you.</i>

343
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:55,934
[Savana]

344
00:22:04,223 --> 00:22:07,960
<i>Everything happens for a reason.</i>

345
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:12,431
<i>What's worse is to spend
the rest of your life with him</i>

346
00:22:12,431 --> 00:22:13,733
<i>and you are not happy.</i>

347
00:22:13,733 --> 00:22:18,471
<i>Tomorrow on Captive Hearts,
before Eat Bulaga!</i>

348
00:22:18,471 --> 00:22:20,072
Hey! That's you, Son!

349
00:22:20,072 --> 00:22:22,174
- Come on, Mom.
- Are you an actor now?

350
00:22:22,174 --> 00:22:24,176
How long have you been standing there?

351
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:26,712
You seem to have seen a ghost.

352
00:22:26,712 --> 00:22:29,982
No! I'm watching it with you.

353
00:22:29,982 --> 00:22:33,953
When did you join
the filming of Captive Hearts?

354
00:22:33,953 --> 00:22:37,957
I just happened
to be at their shooting location.

355
00:22:37,957 --> 00:22:40,793
I didn't know
they would drag me into the scene.

356
00:22:40,793 --> 00:22:44,630
And what would I do with it?

357
00:22:46,565 --> 00:22:48,234
Me, Son.

358
00:22:48,234 --> 00:22:51,270
I will ask Savana for a video greeting.

359
00:22:52,571 --> 00:22:54,606
Why?

360
00:22:56,208 --> 00:22:59,077
I'm her super fan.

361
00:23:00,109 --> 00:23:01,659
Yes.

362
00:23:04,317 --> 00:23:07,486
I will make my friends envious.

363
00:23:09,955 --> 00:23:11,591
Why does it seem

364
00:23:11,592 --> 00:23:15,452
like a lot of people are obsessed
with Savana?

365
00:23:18,498 --> 00:23:25,871
She's pretty, kind, and a good actress.

366
00:23:27,646 --> 00:23:29,881
Why? Have you met her?

367
00:23:30,776 --> 00:23:32,900
I haven't yet.

368
00:23:32,901 --> 00:23:41,953
But whenever I see her, I'm so fond of her.

369
00:23:41,954 --> 00:23:48,258
It feels like
I have known her for a long time.

370
00:23:50,229 --> 00:23:55,265
What do you mean by that?

371
00:23:56,736 --> 00:24:02,942
She seems so familiar to me.

372
00:24:02,942 --> 00:24:07,379
I feel like we're close.

373
00:24:09,014 --> 00:24:13,185
She's so familiar to me.

374
00:24:15,087 --> 00:24:17,946
She's the type of woman

375
00:24:17,946 --> 00:24:20,760
<i>whom I will cook your favorite adobo for.</i>

376
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:24,363
A dish I can cook
even when my eyes are closed.

377
00:24:25,664 --> 00:24:29,402
Mom, you're just hungry.

378
00:24:29,402 --> 00:24:31,256
Come on.

379
00:24:32,204 --> 00:24:33,272
I know what to do.

380
00:24:33,272 --> 00:24:36,075
I will cook adobo tomorrow...

381
00:24:36,075 --> 00:24:38,881
For my celebrity son.

382
00:24:41,781 --> 00:24:42,873
I'll leave you for now.

383
00:24:42,873 --> 00:24:47,826
I will call my friends
to tell them to watch Captive Hearts tomorrow.

384
00:24:50,022 --> 00:24:53,893
<i>Everything happens for a reason.</i>

385
00:24:53,893 --> 00:24:59,022
<i>What's worse is
to spend the rest of your life...</i>

386
00:25:04,069 --> 00:25:05,671
<i>Why do you want to kill me?</i>

387
00:25:05,671 --> 00:25:09,575
<i>What? Have you forgotten about me?</i>

388
00:25:09,575 --> 00:25:12,778
<i>That's how rich people are.</i>

389
00:25:12,778 --> 00:25:15,848
<i>You look at poor people like cockroaches...</i>

390
00:25:15,848 --> 00:25:18,784
He seldom spoke when we were in college.

391
00:25:18,784 --> 00:25:23,689
Well, they say silent people are more scary.

392
00:25:23,689 --> 00:25:28,105
<i>I'm old enough! I won't lose anything.</i>

393
00:25:52,510 --> 00:25:54,050
What are you watching, Love?

394
00:25:54,050 --> 00:25:57,090
You look so affected.

395
00:25:57,090 --> 00:25:59,059
Is it good?

396
00:25:59,059 --> 00:26:00,360
What?

397
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:02,719
The one you're watching.

398
00:26:05,198 --> 00:26:06,733
It's okay,

399
00:26:06,734 --> 00:26:09,703
but I dislike
how the leading man portrays his character.

400
00:26:11,039 --> 00:26:13,790
When did you start watching TV series?

401
00:26:15,009 --> 00:26:17,679
Well... Are you okay? Are you ready?

402
00:26:17,679 --> 00:26:18,913
Let's go?

403
00:26:18,913 --> 00:26:21,849
Why? Are you hungry?
Do you want me to order food?

404
00:26:21,849 --> 00:26:23,351
Love.

405
00:26:23,351 --> 00:26:25,186
You forgot again.

406
00:26:25,186 --> 00:26:27,955
I don't eat at this time. See?

407
00:26:27,955 --> 00:26:32,094
- Intermittent fasting, remember?
- Yeah, right.

408
00:26:33,027 --> 00:26:35,029
Love, thank you.

409
00:26:35,029 --> 00:26:38,465
Is it really okay that you went out with me?

410
00:26:39,217 --> 00:26:41,318
Are you not in a bad mood?

411
00:26:42,370 --> 00:26:45,089
Bad mood? Why?

412
00:26:46,107 --> 00:26:49,636
When you're busy,
you're always in a bad mood.

413
00:26:52,177 --> 00:26:53,938
Is it really okay with you?

414
00:26:54,594 --> 00:26:57,518
Yeah. Of course. No problem.

415
00:26:57,518 --> 00:26:59,654
Thank you, Love!

416
00:26:59,654 --> 00:27:04,525
I think it's a blessing in disguise
that you took leave from Casa Fuerte.

417
00:27:04,525 --> 00:27:07,028
What do you mean?

418
00:27:07,028 --> 00:27:09,664
We have more quality time together.

419
00:27:09,664 --> 00:27:11,366
Right?

420
00:27:15,647 --> 00:27:19,474
Another day is another day!

421
00:27:19,474 --> 00:27:24,383
Mirror, mirror, on the wall,
who's the fairest of them all?

422
00:27:25,012 --> 00:27:27,206
It's you, Miss Via!

423
00:27:27,206 --> 00:27:29,470
A beautiful morning!

424
00:27:31,319 --> 00:27:32,854
Queenie!

425
00:27:32,854 --> 00:27:34,789
I love your energy.

426
00:27:34,789 --> 00:27:38,092
- Thank you, Miss Via.
- Looks like you had good coffee.

427
00:27:38,092 --> 00:27:40,094
Is everything set?
Have you checked everything?

428
00:27:40,094 --> 00:27:41,389
- Yes, Miss Via!
- Okay.

429
00:27:41,389 --> 00:27:44,832
Our vlog interview for today
is just a mini challenge.

430
00:27:44,832 --> 00:27:48,890
Speaking of, our guest is here.

431
00:28:33,881 --> 00:28:38,619
Savana, you're currently
on top of your league.

432
00:28:38,619 --> 00:28:42,223
Hailed as the Primetime Duchess
of Philippine TV,

433
00:28:42,223 --> 00:28:45,718
Back-to-back Box Office Queen!

434
00:28:45,718 --> 00:28:48,575
What else could Savana ever ask for?

435
00:28:50,044 --> 00:28:54,368
I want to travel to Europe.

436
00:28:54,368 --> 00:28:55,770
Paris.

437
00:28:55,770 --> 00:28:57,236
Paris!

438
00:28:57,236 --> 00:28:59,339
The fashion capital.

439
00:28:59,339 --> 00:29:04,510
So, I assume
you're also into designer brands?

440
00:29:05,778 --> 00:29:07,110
No.

441
00:29:08,748 --> 00:29:10,483
The culture.

442
00:29:10,483 --> 00:29:12,518
I want to experience the culture.

443
00:29:12,518 --> 00:29:16,022
That's why I want to go there so badly.

444
00:29:16,022 --> 00:29:21,627
Whenever I hear that place,
there's unexplainable magic for me.

445
00:29:23,129 --> 00:29:28,918
But fashion, I mean,
it's also part of the Parisian culture.

446
00:29:29,769 --> 00:29:34,402
I'm not into luxury things ever since.

447
00:29:35,230 --> 00:29:38,558
I don't want the overhyped brands.

448
00:29:39,946 --> 00:29:43,916
I have endorsements, a lot, yes.

449
00:29:43,916 --> 00:29:49,822
But I make sure that all the brands I endorse
are accessible to everyone.

450
00:29:49,822 --> 00:29:53,292
So you have this thing for ordinary people?

451
00:29:53,292 --> 00:29:56,207
Oppressed people.

452
00:29:57,269 --> 00:29:59,957
Those who are in need.

453
00:30:01,034 --> 00:30:07,507
I promised from the very start to give voice

454
00:30:07,507 --> 00:30:12,347
to the people who aren't given
a chance to fight.

455
00:30:13,508 --> 00:30:16,044
Those who are at the bottom.

456
00:30:17,216 --> 00:30:22,988
For example,
people whose lands have been grabbed.

457
00:30:27,627 --> 00:30:30,196
That's impressive, Savana.

458
00:30:30,196 --> 00:30:33,833
Maybe your fans admire you

459
00:30:33,833 --> 00:30:36,002
because you're not just a pretty face.

460
00:30:36,002 --> 00:30:38,237
You're also a woman of substance.

461
00:30:38,237 --> 00:30:39,702
That's good.

462
00:30:40,673 --> 00:30:45,545
It's a shame if we don't use
our influence rightly, isn't it?

463
00:30:45,545 --> 00:30:48,748
I agree with you. 100 percent.

464
00:30:48,748 --> 00:30:51,117
I think that's it!

465
00:30:51,117 --> 00:30:53,720
- We're done?
- Yeah, we're done!

466
00:30:53,720 --> 00:30:55,354
Via, thank you so much.

467
00:30:55,354 --> 00:30:58,024
Thank you so much for your time too.

468
00:30:58,024 --> 00:31:01,094
Thank you. I appreciate it.

469
00:31:01,094 --> 00:31:05,098
We're done. We're okay, right, Queenie?

470
00:31:05,098 --> 00:31:06,499
Yes, okay. Pack up!

471
00:31:06,499 --> 00:31:08,267
Everything's okay? I leave everyone to you.

472
00:31:08,267 --> 00:31:09,697
- Yes, Miss Via.
- Where's your assistant?

473
00:31:09,697 --> 00:31:11,704
Shoot.

474
00:31:11,704 --> 00:31:13,740
She's waiting for me in the lobby.

475
00:31:14,941 --> 00:31:16,446
Love.

476
00:31:20,761 --> 00:31:24,897
Savana, I want you
to meet Liam, my boyfriend.

477
00:31:30,716 --> 00:31:32,805
Liam Herrera.

478
00:31:37,543 --> 00:31:39,490
You know each other?

479
00:31:43,002 --> 00:31:46,249
He was at my filming the other day.

480
00:31:48,434 --> 00:31:51,201
You were at Savana's filming, Love?

481
00:31:54,550 --> 00:31:56,682
Yeah.

482
00:31:56,682 --> 00:31:59,675
Actually, I just passed by their location.

483
00:32:00,670 --> 00:32:04,906
You didn't tell me that you've met.

484
00:32:07,493 --> 00:32:09,428
So, better, I guess.

485
00:32:09,428 --> 00:32:12,665
Love, is it okay for you
to walk Savana to the lobby?

486
00:32:12,665 --> 00:32:14,967
Her assistant's there.

487
00:32:14,967 --> 00:32:16,402
I'm so sorry, I can't bring you there.

488
00:32:16,402 --> 00:32:19,605
I still need to supervise the photo shoot.

489
00:32:19,605 --> 00:32:20,940
Thank you again for your time.

490
00:32:20,940 --> 00:32:22,575
Thanks, too.

491
00:32:22,575 --> 00:32:23,810
Queenie, let's go?

492
00:32:23,810 --> 00:32:25,477
Yes, Ma'am.

493
00:32:37,690 --> 00:32:39,547
Savana, wait.

494
00:32:45,765 --> 00:32:47,992
You know my full name?

495
00:32:49,635 --> 00:32:52,458
You were my classmate in Philo 101.

496
00:32:54,106 --> 00:32:56,309
Yes, that's right.

497
00:32:56,309 --> 00:32:58,075
Classmate.

498
00:32:58,945 --> 00:33:00,680
How are you, classmate?

499
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:02,786
You're in the news.

500
00:33:04,921 --> 00:33:08,524
You're an executive in Casa Fuerte.

501
00:33:09,622 --> 00:33:13,322
And you grabbed the land
of Verde Village's residents, right?

502
00:33:15,561 --> 00:33:17,630
I don't have anything to do with that.

503
00:33:17,630 --> 00:33:21,099
It's your company.
And you don't have anything to do with it?

504
00:33:22,668 --> 00:33:25,243
Do I look like I was born yesterday?

505
00:33:27,707 --> 00:33:32,576
Everything I said in my interview
is all true.

506
00:33:32,576 --> 00:33:36,781
I sympathize with the poor.

507
00:33:36,781 --> 00:33:41,685
If you knew me in college,
you knew I had a difficult life.

508
00:33:41,685 --> 00:33:43,721
And you...

509
00:33:43,721 --> 00:33:46,415
I know you were a scholar.

510
00:33:47,659 --> 00:33:50,395
So I can't understand how you could do that

511
00:33:50,395 --> 00:33:53,498
to the residents of Verde Village.

512
00:33:54,166 --> 00:33:58,270
Whatever our company did, I'm sorry.

513
00:33:58,270 --> 00:34:00,737
You don't need to explain.

514
00:34:02,442 --> 00:34:06,229
I just want to call you out
because what you did is wrong.

515
00:34:07,814 --> 00:34:09,659
Good day, Mr. Herrera.

516
00:34:41,348 --> 00:34:43,683
<i>And you, I know you were a scholar.</i>

517
00:34:43,683 --> 00:34:46,353
<i>So I can't understand how you could do that</i>

518
00:34:46,353 --> 00:34:48,866
<i>to the residents of Verde Village.</i>

519
00:35:12,846 --> 00:35:15,414
Here. You can have it.

520
00:35:16,983 --> 00:35:18,918
Wow. Thanks, Bro.

521
00:35:44,244 --> 00:35:46,346
Don't look at her so much.

522
00:35:46,346 --> 00:35:49,349
She won't come down for you.

523
00:35:49,349 --> 00:35:51,751
Come on. I just find her beautiful.

524
00:35:53,820 --> 00:35:55,155
Have some of this.

525
00:35:55,155 --> 00:35:56,722
No, you can have it.

526
00:36:01,895 --> 00:36:05,265
Of all people who look at that billboard,

527
00:36:05,265 --> 00:36:07,874
you're the only one who looks sad.

528
00:36:09,369 --> 00:36:11,705
Some even took photos of themselves with it.

529
00:36:11,705 --> 00:36:13,773
They're so happy.

530
00:36:13,773 --> 00:36:15,342
They find her so beautiful.

531
00:36:15,342 --> 00:36:17,977
Well, she really is beautiful, anyway.

532
00:36:19,746 --> 00:36:24,150
Well, maybe that's how it goes. Right, Bro?

533
00:36:24,150 --> 00:36:28,252
She's up there, and you're down here.

534
00:36:29,189 --> 00:36:32,861
You can't deny the distance
between you and her.

535
00:36:34,909 --> 00:36:38,345
Do you also watch Joyce's TV show?

536
00:36:39,733 --> 00:36:41,538
Who is Joyce?

537
00:36:42,803 --> 00:36:45,397
Savana, she's my wife.

538
00:36:46,339 --> 00:36:48,413
Right, Love?

539
00:36:50,249 --> 00:36:52,045
Love, are you hungry?

540
00:36:52,045 --> 00:36:53,513
Let's eat.

541
00:36:53,513 --> 00:36:55,715
My good friend here gave us food.

542
00:36:55,715 --> 00:36:57,202
What's your name, Bro?

543
00:37:02,288 --> 00:37:05,358
I'm glad you came back to your senses.

544
00:37:06,292 --> 00:37:09,094
I thought I was no longer
part of Casa Fuerte.

545
00:37:09,094 --> 00:37:11,630
Why did you call me here?

546
00:37:11,630 --> 00:37:13,866
You're right.

547
00:37:13,866 --> 00:37:18,107
You're no longer part of Casa Fuerte
because of what you did.

548
00:37:19,238 --> 00:37:21,673
You know what, Liam?

549
00:37:21,673 --> 00:37:30,215
Our critics see us as
a heartless corporation...

550
00:37:31,183 --> 00:37:39,183
Tough, unwavering, showing no weakness.

551
00:37:41,527 --> 00:37:43,256
What do they know?

552
00:37:44,396 --> 00:37:51,703
Our name, Herrera, means iron works.

553
00:37:52,571 --> 00:37:54,444
Foundry.

554
00:37:55,274 --> 00:37:59,511
Metal that is being molded under high heat.

555
00:37:59,511 --> 00:38:02,507
Pounded to be firm.

556
00:38:04,883 --> 00:38:10,250
Because you can't be soft-hearted
in business.

557
00:38:10,250 --> 00:38:13,155
You need to have iron hands.

558
00:38:16,261 --> 00:38:19,416
That's why a lot will be surprised
by what I'll do.

559
00:38:21,466 --> 00:38:24,611
So I'm giving you a second chance, Liam.

560
00:38:26,371 --> 00:38:28,972
Are you going to reinstate me in Casa Fuerte?

561
00:38:30,309 --> 00:38:32,211
No.

562
00:38:32,211 --> 00:38:36,081
But I'm going to put you
in one of our other companies.

563
00:38:36,081 --> 00:38:38,730
In Blacksmith Productions.

564
00:38:42,121 --> 00:38:45,091
Isn't that Vergil's production house?

565
00:38:45,091 --> 00:38:46,559
Yes.

566
00:38:46,559 --> 00:38:49,461
Why? Is there a problem with that?

567
00:38:51,998 --> 00:38:55,434
No, Dad. But what am I going to do there?

568
00:38:55,434 --> 00:38:57,570
I made you study engineering
after your first degree.

569
00:38:57,570 --> 00:39:00,239
But you wasted it.

570
00:39:00,239 --> 00:39:04,944
I offered you to work
at our construction company many times.

571
00:39:04,944 --> 00:39:07,780
But you turned me down.

572
00:39:07,780 --> 00:39:13,072
Now, you can do whatever you want
in Blacksmith.

573
00:39:15,922 --> 00:39:20,092
But once the situation
in Casa Fuerte becomes okay

574
00:39:20,092 --> 00:39:23,796
and you gain the investors' trust again,

575
00:39:23,796 --> 00:39:25,838
I will reinstate you.

576
00:39:32,705 --> 00:39:38,064
With the way you look,
it seems that you received bad news.

577
00:39:40,146 --> 00:39:42,815
Who would have thought?

578
00:39:42,815 --> 00:39:47,878
Casa Fuerte's wonder boy,
Herrera's prodigal son,

579
00:39:47,878 --> 00:39:49,969
ended up in my company.

580
00:39:52,358 --> 00:39:53,593
Get changed.

581
00:39:53,593 --> 00:39:57,129
Get ready for our meeting
for your first project.

582
00:39:57,129 --> 00:39:59,337
Does it need to be now, Vergil?

583
00:40:00,800 --> 00:40:04,604
From now on, you will call me by my initials.

584
00:40:04,604 --> 00:40:07,974
In Blacksmith, I'm the boss.

585
00:40:07,974 --> 00:40:11,727
You'll address me as VLH.

586
00:40:15,948 --> 00:40:18,718
Hey, you two.

587
00:40:18,718 --> 00:40:22,955
Vergil, make this day productive.

588
00:40:22,955 --> 00:40:25,591
You have a meeting with my good friend.

589
00:40:25,591 --> 00:40:27,522
Don't be late.

590
00:40:29,262 --> 00:40:31,967
Welcome to Blacksmith, Bro.

591
00:40:40,039 --> 00:40:41,506
Via.

592
00:40:44,377 --> 00:40:45,978
Love!

593
00:40:47,913 --> 00:40:49,448
What are you doing here?

594
00:40:49,448 --> 00:40:52,318
My dad told me to come.
He said it was for a meeting.

595
00:40:52,318 --> 00:40:55,454
I think he's taking a movie project.

596
00:40:55,454 --> 00:40:57,123
- Is that right?
- Yes.

597
00:40:57,123 --> 00:40:58,958
And Via will be the head stylist.

598
00:40:58,958 --> 00:41:02,328
She's going to be in charge
of our actors' overall look.

599
00:41:02,328 --> 00:41:04,430
Looks like it's big-budgeted.

600
00:41:05,831 --> 00:41:07,233
Congressman dela Peña!

601
00:41:07,233 --> 00:41:09,135
Vergil.

602
00:41:09,135 --> 00:41:10,101
How are you?

603
00:41:10,101 --> 00:41:13,565
I'm glad my godson,
Tristan's movie project in Blacksmith

604
00:41:13,565 --> 00:41:16,642
will now push through.

605
00:41:16,642 --> 00:41:18,869
It better be a hit.

606
00:41:18,869 --> 00:41:24,021
Tristan's success in the next elections
for congressman

607
00:41:24,021 --> 00:41:25,918
depends on that film.

608
00:41:25,918 --> 00:41:28,154
What can I say?

609
00:41:28,154 --> 00:41:31,122
He looks up to his godfather so much.

610
00:41:31,122 --> 00:41:32,469
Of course, Uncle Ramon.

611
00:41:32,469 --> 00:41:37,263
Well, everything depends
on the creative manager of Tristan's movie.

612
00:41:37,263 --> 00:41:38,864
That's Liam.

613
00:41:41,734 --> 00:41:43,769
So...

614
00:41:43,769 --> 00:41:46,872
This is where Danilo dumped you.

615
00:41:46,872 --> 00:41:48,307
Dad.

616
00:41:52,745 --> 00:41:56,181
I'm excited to meet my next leading lady.

617
00:41:57,081 --> 00:41:58,979
Shall we?

618
00:41:58,979 --> 00:42:00,519
After you, son.

619
00:42:00,519 --> 00:42:02,020
Let's go.

620
00:42:22,808 --> 00:42:26,479
And after all the oppression
the mayor has done,

621
00:42:26,479 --> 00:42:29,081
Leon will rise up from the dead

622
00:42:29,081 --> 00:42:36,788
to save his beloved Jackie
and free his fellowmen.

623
00:42:38,424 --> 00:42:40,359
That's the end of the presentation.

624
00:43:00,579 --> 00:43:02,081
What do you think?

625
00:43:02,081 --> 00:43:08,053
It's an exciting story,
and I can feel the significance of my role.

626
00:43:08,053 --> 00:43:09,955
Wait, how many fight scenes will I have
in the movie?

627
00:43:11,237 --> 00:43:14,125
Three fight scenes, two car chases,

628
00:43:14,125 --> 00:43:18,151
and one long-take rooftop chase
where goons will gang up on you.

629
00:43:18,151 --> 00:43:21,833
Plus, a fight scene while in a helicopter.

630
00:43:23,135 --> 00:43:25,304
Action-packed!

631
00:43:25,304 --> 00:43:28,207
Do I have a love scene here?

632
00:43:28,207 --> 00:43:30,158
What a narcissist.

633
00:43:31,243 --> 00:43:39,183
Vergil, the plot is somehow similar
to my recent film, Tough Guy.

634
00:43:39,183 --> 00:43:43,704
Instead of a politician,

635
00:43:43,704 --> 00:43:46,225
can the villain be a businessman?

636
00:43:46,225 --> 00:43:47,960
We don't want to ruffle feathers.

637
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:49,295
No problem, Congressman.

638
00:43:49,295 --> 00:43:51,130
The details are not set in stone.

639
00:43:51,130 --> 00:43:53,466
It can still change.

640
00:43:53,466 --> 00:43:57,536
Good thing Liam is here
to take note of the revisions.

641
00:43:57,536 --> 00:43:59,337
Right, Liam?

642
00:44:04,877 --> 00:44:05,878
Good.

643
00:44:05,878 --> 00:44:10,715
Okay, so... Savana, what do you think?

644
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:17,990
I need time to think.

645
00:44:17,990 --> 00:44:19,925
Excuse me.

646
00:44:24,005 --> 00:44:26,331
Excuse me. Excuse me for a while.

647
00:44:47,493 --> 00:44:49,027
Savana.

648
00:44:50,623 --> 00:44:53,997
Savana, what drama is this?

649
00:44:56,095 --> 00:44:58,830
I won't do that project, Mom.

650
00:45:00,399 --> 00:45:02,033
Why?

651
00:45:03,936 --> 00:45:06,171
The story isn't good.

652
00:45:07,640 --> 00:45:09,141
Oh, come on.

653
00:45:09,141 --> 00:45:12,211
When did you become picky with projects?

654
00:45:12,211 --> 00:45:14,866
- I won't do it.
- What do you mean?

655
00:45:14,866 --> 00:45:16,982
Tell me why.

656
00:45:20,352 --> 00:45:24,823
Mom, it's because...
Because of Liam and Vergil Herrera.

657
00:45:25,457 --> 00:45:29,060
They're the ones
who grabbed the lands in Verde Village.

658
00:45:29,828 --> 00:45:32,012
What do we have to do with that?

659
00:45:32,012 --> 00:45:33,598
Why?

660
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:39,169
You know how it feels
to not have a permanent home, Mom.

661
00:45:40,205 --> 00:45:43,074
We get kicked out every month.

662
00:45:43,976 --> 00:45:49,381
And now you want me
to work with those opportunists?

663
00:45:49,381 --> 00:45:52,985
Why? Did they take away your house?

664
00:45:52,985 --> 00:45:55,154
What about my advocacies?

665
00:45:55,154 --> 00:45:57,033
We both know that from the very start,

666
00:45:57,033 --> 00:46:00,459
all I want is to help the oppressed.

667
00:46:00,459 --> 00:46:03,963
Why? Are you planning to run for Congress?

668
00:46:03,963 --> 00:46:05,931
- God, Savana.
- Mom, please listen to me!

669
00:46:05,931 --> 00:46:08,867
No, you listen to me!

670
00:46:08,867 --> 00:46:11,168
If you don't want to lose your house

671
00:46:11,168 --> 00:46:14,821
like the informal settlers you're defending,

672
00:46:14,821 --> 00:46:16,241
go back inside.

673
00:46:16,241 --> 00:46:20,679
Smile and tell them you love the project!

674
00:46:22,581 --> 00:46:25,751
I'll be a hypocrite if I do that, Mom.

675
00:46:25,751 --> 00:46:29,020
I won't work with the Herreras.

676
00:46:30,823 --> 00:46:32,858
You can't back out anymore.

677
00:46:32,858 --> 00:46:36,865
You already signed a contract with Blacksmith

678
00:46:36,865 --> 00:46:39,365
even before the news about Casa Fuerte
broke out.

679
00:46:39,365 --> 00:46:42,033
I can buy my contract.

680
00:46:43,133 --> 00:46:45,269
Listen to me.

681
00:46:46,939 --> 00:46:50,241
This is a big project.

682
00:46:50,241 --> 00:46:55,171
Congressman dela Peña handpicked you
to become the leading lady of this film.

683
00:46:55,171 --> 00:46:57,397
He's an influential man.

684
00:46:58,349 --> 00:47:02,093
Now, I'll give you two choices. You choose.

685
00:47:02,093 --> 00:47:06,827
You'll finish this project
and still have your career,

686
00:47:06,827 --> 00:47:10,462
or you'll go down.

687
00:47:17,336 --> 00:47:19,170
Wrong timing.

688
00:47:22,174 --> 00:47:25,978
Savana won't accept this project anymore.

689
00:47:25,978 --> 00:47:28,513
What made you say that?

690
00:47:29,613 --> 00:47:33,517
- I just feel it.
- We know other actresses.

691
00:47:33,517 --> 00:47:36,433
Oh, anyway, who knows, Congressman...

692
00:47:36,433 --> 00:47:38,256
It's a go.

693
00:47:38,994 --> 00:47:40,378
Good!

694
00:47:43,396 --> 00:47:45,829
I'm glad you accepted the project.

695
00:47:45,829 --> 00:47:47,964
We'll have so much fun.

696
00:47:51,835 --> 00:47:55,939
Looking forward to working with you,
Congressman dela Peña.

697
00:47:55,939 --> 00:47:58,371
The pleasure is mine, dear.

698
00:47:59,243 --> 00:48:02,332
I'm excited to work with you, Savana.

699
00:48:02,332 --> 00:48:06,650
Us, too.
We're excited to work with Blacksmith.

700
00:48:06,650 --> 00:48:08,285
Oh, okay?

701
00:48:08,285 --> 00:48:10,220
Thank you very much.

702
00:48:12,793 --> 00:48:14,932
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

703
00:48:23,835 --> 00:48:27,638
I didn't expect that Savana
would accept that project.

704
00:48:28,306 --> 00:48:29,774
Why, Boss Bro?

705
00:48:29,774 --> 00:48:32,643
It's work.

706
00:48:33,378 --> 00:48:35,446
I don't know. Something feels off.

707
00:48:35,446 --> 00:48:36,781
Off?

708
00:48:36,781 --> 00:48:38,766
Who wrote that story?

709
00:48:38,766 --> 00:48:40,919
It's so unconvincing.

710
00:48:40,919 --> 00:48:42,124
Leave it be.

711
00:48:42,983 --> 00:48:47,936
Just be grateful that Señor Danilo
didn't fire you after what happened.

712
00:48:48,726 --> 00:48:50,728
But he made me work for my brother.

713
00:48:50,728 --> 00:48:52,630
It's only my first day,
but I want to resign already.

714
00:48:52,630 --> 00:48:55,066
Don't you ever think about that.

715
00:48:55,066 --> 00:48:58,069
Isn't this what you want?

716
00:48:58,069 --> 00:49:00,638
To make a film?

717
00:49:00,638 --> 00:49:04,742
- This is your chance, Boss Bro.
- Not this kind of movie, Borj.

718
00:49:04,742 --> 00:49:09,081
And I can't stand Tristan Perez.

719
00:49:09,914 --> 00:49:12,483
He has an annoying presence.

720
00:49:12,483 --> 00:49:13,484
Right?

721
00:49:13,484 --> 00:49:14,752
You're so silly.

722
00:49:16,888 --> 00:49:19,657
- But what about you, Borj?
- What?

723
00:49:19,657 --> 00:49:22,660
How are you in Casa Fuerte?

724
00:49:23,728 --> 00:49:29,033
I'm currently doing nothing.

725
00:49:30,501 --> 00:49:31,936
Doing nothing?

726
00:49:31,936 --> 00:49:34,739
You mean you're no longer in Casa Fuerte?

727
00:49:34,739 --> 00:49:36,474
Yes.

728
00:49:36,474 --> 00:49:40,878
What's the use of being an assistant
if I have no one to assist, right?

729
00:49:41,813 --> 00:49:46,851
Then you can be my assistant in Blacksmith.

730
00:49:46,851 --> 00:49:49,219
Don't kid me like that, Boss Bro.

731
00:49:49,219 --> 00:49:50,630
You know what I'll say.

732
00:49:50,630 --> 00:49:53,091
Don't you want it? I won't force you.

733
00:49:53,091 --> 00:49:55,627
No, I'll take the job.

734
00:49:55,627 --> 00:49:57,528
- Are you sure?
- Yes!

735
00:49:57,528 --> 00:49:58,630
- Game!
- Maybe you don't want it.

736
00:49:58,630 --> 00:49:59,930
- Just forget about it.
- No, no, no.

737
00:49:59,930 --> 00:50:01,260
- Let's go.
- Hey.

738
00:50:01,260 --> 00:50:03,301
- Thank you, Boss Bro!
- Take it easy.

739
00:50:03,301 --> 00:50:04,835
- Take it easy.
- Thank you!

740
00:50:07,138 --> 00:50:08,539
Do you want coffee?

741
00:50:08,539 --> 00:50:09,740
- Will you pay for it?
- Yes, it's on me.

742
00:50:09,740 --> 00:50:11,643
- Sure. Buy me coffee.
- Boss Bro!

743
00:50:11,643 --> 00:50:13,077
You keep putting your arm on my shoulder.

744
00:50:13,077 --> 00:50:14,379
Come on, Boss Bro. Let's have coffee!

745
00:50:14,379 --> 00:50:15,280
I won't put my arm on your shoulders anymore.

746
00:50:15,280 --> 00:50:17,582
- Go that way.
- I'll buy you coffee.

747
00:50:17,582 --> 00:50:19,296
If you'll pay for it.

748
00:50:29,861 --> 00:50:32,230
Helpless Cindy thanks her savior.

749
00:50:32,230 --> 00:50:35,366
Stop. That's not right.

750
00:50:35,366 --> 00:50:36,567
I need no saving.

751
00:50:36,567 --> 00:50:39,037
We, women, need no saving.

752
00:50:39,037 --> 00:50:40,538
I won't leave you here.

753
00:50:40,538 --> 00:50:41,466
I said go.

754
00:50:41,467 --> 00:50:44,442
I won't go anywhere because I love you!

755
00:50:44,442 --> 00:50:46,945
This is Liam's second favorite.

756
00:50:46,945 --> 00:50:48,500
My mom likes you a lot.

757
00:50:48,501 --> 00:50:50,466
Looks like she's upstaging you.

758
00:50:50,467 --> 00:50:52,571
It seems that she wants to audition
as a daughter-in-law.

759
00:50:52,571 --> 00:50:54,196
So controlling.

760
00:50:54,196 --> 00:50:54,834
Who?

761
00:50:54,834 --> 00:50:57,423
My mom's so controlling

762
00:50:57,424 --> 00:51:03,360
and a terror manager.

763
00:51:15,799 --> 00:51:16,868
Oh my, crocodile!

764
00:51:16,868 --> 00:51:19,410
Have you been here long?

765
00:51:19,410 --> 00:51:23,848
This story has to have a magic typewriter.

766
00:51:23,848 --> 00:51:24,601
What?

767
00:51:24,601 --> 00:51:29,987
The magical typewriter
is the reason why they got separated!
